{%- comment -%}
  Template for the policy pages that used to live at /policies/*.

  Those are rendered by Shopify itself and can only be edited as one plain
  rich-text box in Settings > Policies -- no sections, no page editor. Moving
  the content into real pages makes them editable like any other page.

  The markup here deliberately reproduces Shopify's own policy DOM
  (.shopify-policy__container > .shopify-policy__title/h1 and
  .shopify-policy__body > .rte) so that snippets/policy-page.liquid -- the
  restyler that builds the hero, contents list, callouts and footer -- works
  on it unchanged. Same structure and same text through the same code means
  the design is identical to before, with nothing duplicated.

  layout/theme.liquid adds the `template-policy` body class for this suffix,
  which is what that snippet's CSS is scoped to, and renders the snippet.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="shopify-policy__container">
  <div class="shopify-policy__title">
    <h1>{{ page.title }}</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="shopify-policy__body">
    <div class="rte">
      {{ page.content }}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
